     <h1 class="title" title="Mussoorie Hill Station">Mussoorie</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">
<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/north-india-hill-stations/Mussorie-hill-station.jpg" title="Mussoorie hill station" alt="Mussoorie hill station, hill stations in india, north india hill stations, Mussoorie" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


<b>Location:</b> Garhwal Hills,  Uttaranchal<br />
<b>Area:</b> 129sq.Kms<br />
<b>Significance:</b> Queen of  Hillstation.<br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 2500m above sea level.<br />
<b>Climate:</b> Summer 25&#176;C-30&#176;C
Winter 7.2&#176;C-1.1&#176;C .<br/>
<b>Best Time to Visit:</b>  April-June and September-October</p>    
 <p><b>Main Attractions:</b> Mussorrie Mall, Nag Devta Temple,  </p> 

<p><b>Queen of Hills</b>, Mussoorie is a hill situated at the foot of the beautiful <b>Himalayan ranges</b> from Uttarakhand. The atmosphere here is quite cool and pleasant, has a height of 6600 feet of a charming hill town has locked the <b>snow-capped mountains</b> in the north-east and Doon Valley Shiwalik and areas to the south. The green hills are a wide range of flora and fauna. Visiting Address Mussoorie is an experience <b>wonderland for tourists</b>. Nature has blessed Mussoorie is a pine forest on the sea covered hills, snowy mountains and the man has enhanced the beauty of modern bungalows, malls and a garden. All these are enough to attract any tourist. The charming hill station is a good escape the heat of the plains. Mussoorie attracts couples on their honeymoon, because it's cool, calm and beautiful environment. They enjoyed a romantic stroll jewels of nature breaks the camel's back Road.</p>

<strong>Sight seeing in Mussoorie </strong>

<p>Mussoorie has a lot of beautiful sights, and tourists will start pouring with summer. Boating, and many small waterfalls in the area <b>Kempty river</b> rises in the lake of fog to make the picnic more natural wannabe. <b>Municipal Garden</b> is another picnic in miniature <b>artificial lake</b> where pedal system is available in the middle of a green carpet-kept garden. Mussoorie Lake is a place for a picnic also developed relatively recently with the installation pedaled boats. It provides an enchanting view of <b>Doon Valley</b> and nearby villages. Bhatta Falls, Fall Fall Jharipani moves and a great place for the enjoyment of water and a picnic. The <b>highest peak of Mussoorie</b>, childern Lodge is located near Lal Tibbo taking on the snow-covered mountains is exhilarating. <b>Gunhill</b> is the second highest point in Mussoorie which gun was used in the past to probe at noon. </p>

<p><b>Nag Devta temple</b> dedicated to Shiva and the temple atop the hill Jwalaji Benog dedicated to the <b>goddess Durga</b> is also worth a visit. The temple of the goddess Durga offers wonderful views over the river valley Aglare. Peace and serenity found at the end Cloud is divine. Its beautiful Himalayan cedar forests have dense flora and fauna, originally built by a major UK is now a hotel, Van. <b>Chetna Kendra</b> is a place for a picnic in the midst of pine forests with shrubs and flowers, wildlife as Ghurair, Himalayan Monal etc. Kakar Benog the sanctuary of the peacock is an ancient sanctuary of mountain quail is spread over 339 hectares a bird house mountain quail (Pahari Bater). Church of Santa Maria is the oldest church in the Himalayas situated at Mussoorie. <b>Kempty tomb</b> is a place to picnic. Garden of the company, the <b>first Tibetan temple</b> built in India, <b>Happy Valley</b>, near Mussoorie Dhanaulti with the track India's largest roller is a must.</p>

<strong>Shopping in Mussoorie</strong>

<p><b>Mussoorie Mall</b> is the place of first-class shopping. You can buy wood decorative items and gifts, copper statues, ceramic vases, wooden boxes, Tibetan prayer wheels and hand-carved oak stick here. Pure Ladakhi Shawls and Jamawar shawls are so old they would buy a bit expensive but worth it really for the money. <b>Himalayan Weavers</b> aims to create a market for artisans of the Himalayan region to sell their products. It is located 8 km. Mussoorie on Mussoorie Dhanaulti Road. Here they produce hand-woven shawls, stoles, scarves and use only natural dyes and wool, silk and pashmina IRA.</p>




